Chuck is the [[Org/The Harlequins/index|Harlequin]] servant assigned to the Party's berth aboard the [[Org/The Harlequins/Providence|Providence]]. He wears the pinstriped clothes of his order under a cape and carries a scepter, and he answers to any name, having told the Party to call him Butler or Thing; they settled on Chuck. He appears as a big brown cat.

He walks his guests through growing a [[Phenomena/Hearts|Heart]] from a [[Phenomena/Keystone|keystone]], is quick to bow and vanish in a puff of smoke, and gave the Party a small figurine of himself that summons him when it is crushed. He carries them about the strider on a floating disc of black stone and says he cannot teach the spell, since he is a sorcerer and the magic is inborn. He acknowledges the gods but does not worship as the Party does. He says he is of little use away from the strider, and offered to have their car lowered off it whenever they wish to leave.
